with open source community it's  there on github and you'll see us you  know adding new features adding better  performance and so on over time and and  that job is essentially never gonna be  done because you know the cloud is never  really done a little quick note at the  end on what we see as the future of  micro virtual or or micro VMs IO  performance and scalability continues to  be a challenge the approach of having a  software vmm means that we are currently  you know implementing virtio in software  and and you know we are have a lot of  room to improve that software and our  planning too but it's always going to be  something of a challenge and so what we  need is the i/o performance and  scalability offered by offload like we  do in ec2 with the nitro system but at  the at the same density that we need to  run serverless scheduling especially you  know at these high densities is is a  challenge around tale latency especially  as you try and drive up CPU utilization  and and I think there's some real  research opportunities there and  industrial development opportunities  we're working with the formal methods  community to to prove some more of the  security properties of fire cracker  and and be able to have you know even  more confidence in in the security of  some of the some of the paths through  that code and there's some really  interesting work that can go in on there  in into research into formal methods  they're a bunch of features that we  would like to see implemented in  firecracker some of which we're working  on ourselves already like snapshots and  ballooning but but also also lots of  opportunities for building you know more  features to - into this micro VM and one  thing I'm really excited about the space  is the rest the mmm project what we've  done with rest VM in partnership with  folks like Intel is is take some of the  core pieces of of fire cracker break  those out into a set of libraries for  building VMs in in the rest programming  language and we've already seen folks  build you know stuff like cloud HV on  top of that recipe mmm core and recipe  mmm is this this essentially growing you  know library or toolkit for building VMs  in in in rest and it's all open source  it's all available and I think it's the  beginning of something that is is really  great trend towards you know mission  mission specific you know micro VMs and  isolation and we're also excited to  continue working with the container  community to you know raise the bar for  container security for everybody  everywhere thank you I've been mark  broker I will you know be happy to  answer your questions
 

